/-! ## The derived tier: stored values, walk checkpoints, and ties

The certificate read's derived objects — the shifted profiles, the
stripped termwise and boundary comparison objects, and the jet's
objects with the slope object — enter as stored values.  Each
substitution walk is verified at suffix checkpoints: `segFold`
folds a stated segment onto the checkpoint below it, `shGo_append`
composes the segments, and the object ties pin each stored value
to its derivation at the stored shifts, so every kernel obligation
is one bounded read of literal-backed data.  The tie decides are
the module's elaboration weight, the certificate data's kernel
re-verification at the stated values. -/

set_option maxRecDepth 8192

/-- The substitution walk's segment fold: a stated segment folded
onto a standing tail value, `shGo`'s own recursion at a seed. -/
private def segFold (l : poly.PPoly) (g : poly.PPoly × poly.PPoly) :
    poly.PPoly × poly.PPoly :=
  l.foldr (fun p acc => profAdd ([p], []) (profMul sh1 acc)) g

/-- The walk splits over an append: the front segment folds onto
the tail's walk. -/
private theorem shGo_append : ∀ (l r : poly.PPoly),
    shGo (l ++ r) = segFold l (shGo r)
  | [], _ => rfl
  | p :: l, r => by
    show profAdd ([p], []) (profMul sh1 (shGo (l ++ r)))
      = profAdd ([p], []) (profMul sh1 (segFold l (shGo r)))
    rw [shGo_append l r]

